error_signature: "BadZipFile: File is not a zip file.*codeload.github.com/.*/tar.gz/[0-9a-f]{40}"
root_cause: "Upstream repo has no git tag/release (tagless); conandata uses a bare codeload commit URL https://codeload.github.com/<owner>/<repo>/tar.gz/<sha> whose basename has no .tar.gz extension, so Conan tools.files.get() mis-detects the format and tries to unzip -> BadZipFile. Use the official GitHub archive URL https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/archive/<sha>.tar.gz which ends in .tar.gz, 302-redirects to the identical codeload commit archive, and carries the same SHA-256."
rec_approach: "official-github-archive-url-for-tagless-commit"
match_keywords: ["BadZipFile", "codeload", "archive", "tar.gz", "no tag", "tagless", "commit archive", "conan get"]
error_excerpt: "ERROR: libcorrect/3.5@ohpcd/stable: Error in source() method\n\tget(self, **self.conan_data['sources'], strip_root=True)\n\tBadZipFile: File is not a zip file"
severity: P1
category: conan, source-download, tagless
last_updated: 2026-09-27
similar_to: ["E276", "E483"]
boundary_novelty: "E276/E483 cover codeload TAG URLs (refs/tags/vX.Y.Z) fixed via get(filename=...); this entry covers TAGLESS commit archives fixed via official GitHub archive URL rewrite (no tag to reference, URL can carry .tar.gz). E483 fallback claimed the codeload URL cannot be rewritten; the official archive URL is the feasible equivalent."